<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Water_VFX">Water VFX</span></h2>
<p>Very fast-flowing water can produce a foamy surface and sprays of droplets that are best simulated using <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/VFX%20editor" title="VFX">VFX</a>. Fountains and waterfalls are the most obvious of these sorts, but you can also use a stream of VFX particles flowing through a streambed to simulate frothy rapids. This sort of usage works well in conjunction with a custom water model underneath the VFX.
</p>
